+All verification complete. The 51 companion full-suite failures are in untouched files (config.test.js, vault-*, fs-lock, chatCreate) and are pre-existing Windows chmod/symlink environment issues (e.g., `0o600` reported as `0o666`, symlink EPERM) — the S40-relevant suites all pass: shell-progress-windowsHide 20/20, skill-install 5/5, outbound-mcp-facade 5/5, chrome-extension 408/408.
+
+## Review summary — s40-quad-m1c
+
+**Verified with tools** (working tree matches m1c patch, base 629580e):
+
+- **Track 1 (ST-4/DL-4/hints)**: `resolveFocusBandSlot` order Confirm→L2→Fleet→thread_tools→L1→empty matches DoD; 56+24≤80px budget holds; shared `collectRunningTools`/`formatRunningToolsLabel`; DL-4 conflict detection + `conflict_hint_zh`; hints in tool description and note. Tested.
+- **Track 2 (skill_install)**: wired at server.ts:3244, injected via tool-definitions-inject.ts; dest always `getConfigDir()/skills` = `~/.cmspark-agent/skills` (config.ts:17,1009); realpath'd source allowlist; engine zip-slip checks; N1c nits fixed (dead `url` param removed; tautology test now asserts `r.ok === true` + file existence).
+- **Track 3 (shell P1b)**: win32 argv restricted to `.exe`/`.com` — N1/N1b regressions fixed and tested (`shouldUseArgvSpawn` shell.ts:174-215); POSIX builtin set added (N1c nit 1 partial fix); `spawn_mode` in results. Argv mode never reinterprets args — strictly reduces injection surface.
+- **Track 4 (outbound MCP)**: spike plan (P0b locked, P0c partial with live bridge/tray confirm explicitly deferred); fail-closed profile; exfil-class disclosure gate; audit line per call. Facade is scaffold-only — no runtime wiring, so no new attack surface.
+
+**No blocking security regressions found.**
+
+## Nits
+
+1. **companion/src/capability/shell.ts:201-210** — POSIX argv spawn mis-handles `~/path` args (`cat ~/notes.txt` → literal `~/notes.txt` → ENOENT), `FOO=bar cmd` env-prefix (ENOENT on `FOO=bar`), and `$?`/`$$` refs (literal). Doc comment at :168 ("true PE binaries / #! scripts work with shell:false") still overclaims. Suggest rejecting `~`-word-starts and `=`-prefixed first tokens, and noting argv mode in the shell_exec tool description.
+2. **companion/src/skills/skill-install.ts:152-155** — only the *compressed* zip size is capped (25MB); extraction has no decompressed-size/file-count budget (assertDirBudget applies only to the path-dir branch). A 25MB zip bomb can expand unbounded into the user skills root — contradicts the declared "zip/dir size caps" Trust mitigation. Apply assertDirBudget post-extraction.
+3. **companion/src/skills/skill-install.ts:48-70** — `isSkillInstallSourceAllowed` accepts any path containing a `downloads`/`下载` *segment* (e.g. `D:\projects\downloads\...`), looser than the "user Downloads" claim; combined with `use_skill` this forms an ungated .md read chain. Consider binding to homedir/Downloads or Chrome's default.
+4. **companion/src/skills/skill-install.ts:123** — content-branch `dest_path: fs.existsSync(dest) ? dest : root` falls back to root — misleading; return the actual written path.
+5. **companion/tests/skill-install.test.ts** — the zip_path branch is never exercised (stub throws "not implemented"); add a zip test incl. allowlist rejection + size cap. Also no coverage for `detectDownloadConflicts` time/path-differ branches.
+6. **chrome-extension/src/background/downloads-find.ts:185** — `Math.max(limit, 20)` is always 20 (limit clamped ≤20); conflict scan covers only the first 20 filtered matches while the query fetches 50. Harmless but misleading.
+7. **companion/src/server.ts:3244** — `skill_install` (writes to disk + reads Downloads) has no L2 gate, unlike host_write/shell_exec. Surface is bounded and consistent with `record_experience`/`use_skill`, but worth confirming this is intentional.
