+# Pi Review — S40 Quad Track (N1)
+
+I inspected the diff patch, all untracked files, and ran the affected test suites (companion: 40 tests pass; chrome-extension: 31 tests pass). Findings below.
+
+## Verified correct
+
+**Track 1 — ST-4 FocusBand** ✅
+- Priority in `resolveFocusBandSlot` (focus-band-priority.ts:53–110) matches DoD exactly: Confirm → L2 → Fleet (with tools secondary) → `thread_tools` → L1 → empty.
+- `secondaryTools` is mutually exclusive with `secondaryAbort` (never buries 急停) and bounded at `FOCUS_BAND_SECONDARY_MAX_PX` (24px) with primary ≤56px → 80px budget respected.
+- Shared `collectRunningTools`/`formatRunningToolsLabel` (running-tools.ts) dedupes newest-first; ChatView footer refactored onto it. Tests cover all new branches.
+
+**Track 2 — DL-4 conflicts** ✅ `detectDownloadConflicts` flags same-basename size/mtime divergence, trimmed `matches.slice(0, limit)` with `scanLimit = max(limit,20)`, and the tool description + note steer to `skill_install` / `~/.cmspark-agent/skills`. Tests present.
+
+**Track 3 — skill_install** ✅ Dest is always the engine → `getConfigDir()/skills` (= `getUserSkillsRoot()`); verified in skill-engine.ts that `importSkill`/`importSkillFolder`/`importSkillFromPath` all write under `skillsDir`, zip entries are traversal-validated, 25MB cap enforced. No Side Panel entry — injected only as an LLM tool in tool-definitions-inject.ts. `server.ts:3243` wires to the real `skillEngine`.
+
+**Track 4 — outbound MCP Phase 0** ✅ Allowlist forbids shell/cookies/host (tested); exfil class (`get_page_text`, `screenshot`) requires `disclosure_accepted`; audit lines carry no page content/bytes; standalone facade matches "no full WS bridge" scope.
+
+## Blocking issues — Track 4 shell P1b (companion/src/capability/shell.ts)
+
+**B1 — Windows regression for .cmd/.bat and cmd builtins.** `shellExec` (shell.ts:207–211) now prefers `spawn(argv[0], argv.slice(1), {shell:false})` for **every** parseable command under the default `confirm_per_command` policy. On Windows I verified `spawn('npm', …, {shell:false})` → ENOENT (−4058); `npm`/`npx`/`yarn` are `.cmd` shims, and cmd builtins (`echo`, `dir`, `type`, `copy`) aren't executables either — all previously ran under `shell:true`. There is no `process.platform === "win32"` guard. The existing test `shell_exec runs when enabled` (capability-shell-netsec.test.ts:38) passes only because this dev box has Git Bash's `/usr/bin/echo.exe` on PATH (verified) — it would ENOENT on a stock Windows install, so CI here cannot catch the breakage.
+
+**B2 — Quoted Windows paths are corrupted; executed argv ≠ confirmed command.** `tryParseSimpleArgv` treats `\` as an escape inside quotes (shell.ts:143–147), which is POSIX semantics, wrong for Windows paths. Verified: `python "C:\Users\t\script.py" --flag` → `["python","C:Users\tscript.py","--flag"]`. Legit commands ENOENT, and the L2-confirmed command string diverges from the argv actually spawned — a confirmed-vs-executed integrity gap, untested for win32 spawn behavior.
+
+## Nits
+- N1 (downloads-find.ts:216): `endTime || ""` — two distinct files with equal size and missing endTime collapse to one empty string and are **not** flagged as conflicts.
+- N2 (downloads-find.ts:198): `count` reports trimmed length while conflict scanning runs over 20 — the hint can reference matches not present in the returned array.
+- N3 (skill-install.ts:73): content case reports `dest_path: root` when the computed file doesn't exist — harmless but misleading.
+- N4 (skill-install.test.ts): stub engine's `skillsDir` differs from `getUserSkillsRoot()`, so `dest_path` correctness vs. the real engine isn't asserted (manually verified against skill-engine.ts — writes do land in user skills root).
+- N5 (outbound-mcp/facade.ts): `disclosure_accepted` is caller-supplied; fine for a Phase 0 spike, but server-side session enforcement must be added before any real bridge.
+
+VERDICT: REJECT
