+## Pi review — S40 Quad-Track (N1B)
+
+### What I verified
+
+**Track 1 — ST-4 FocusBand** ✅
+- `resolveFocusBandSlot` (focus-band-priority.ts:53–110) order matches DoD exactly: Confirm → L2 → Fleet (tools secondary) → `thread_tools` → L1 → empty; `secondaryTools` is mutually exclusive with `secondaryAbort` (急停 never buried) and bounded by `FOCUS_BAND_SECONDARY_MAX_PX` (24px) under the 80px cap. Tests cover all new branches.
+- Shared `collectRunningTools`/`formatRunningToolsLabel` (running-tools.ts) dedupes newest-first, refactored into ChatView too.
+
+**Track 2 — DL-4 conflict hints** ✅ `detectDownloadConflicts` flags same-basename size/mtime/multi-path divergence; N1's nit (missing endTime collapse) is addressed via the `paths` Set. Tests present; extension suite 408/408 green.
+
+**Track 3 — skill_install** ✅ Dest is always the engine's `skillsDir` = `getConfigDir()/skills`; verified in skill-engine.ts that `importSkill`/`importSkillFolder`/`importSkillFromPath` write only under `skillsDir` with zip-entry traversal validation + 25MB cap. Injected only as an LLM tool (tool-definitions-inject.ts:17), **no Side Panel entry**. New tests pass.
+
+**Track 4 — outbound MCP Phase 0** ✅ Allowlist forbids shell/cookies/host (tested), exfil-class (`get_page_text`, `screenshot`) requires `disclosure_accepted`, audit lines carry no page content, facade is standalone (no WS bridge), spike plan doc present and honest about deferred items.
+
+### Blocking issue — Track 4 win32 `.bat`/`.cmd` regression (incomplete B1 fix)
+
+N1 flagged "Windows regression for .cmd/.bat". The N1B fix handles bare names (`npm`, `echo`, `dir` keep `shell:true`) but **explicitly routes extension-bearing `.bat`/`.cmd` programs into argv mode**:
+
+- `companion/src/capability/shell.ts:183` — `/\.(exe|com|bat|cmd)$/i.test(prog)` → argv mode, with docstring claiming `.bat/.cmd` are "explicit executable path" candidates.
+- Empirically verified on this box (Node v24, win32): `spawn('C:\\x\\setup.bat', ['--flag'], {shell:false})` throws **synchronously EINVAL** — not an async `error` event. `shellExec` (shell.ts:242) has no try/catch around `spawn`, so every `.bat`/`.cmd` command (e.g. `venv\Scripts\activate.bat`, a downloaded `setup.bat --silent`) that ran fine pre-P1b via `shell:true` now returns `{success:false, error:"spawn EINVAL"}`.
+- `companion/src/capability/shell.ts:181` — win32 `policy=allowlist` routes *any* parsed command to argv mode, so allowlisted `npm run build` (a `.cmd` shim) → ENOENT; previously worked via shell.
+- Tests (`shell-progress-windowsHide.test.ts`) only assert the *decision function* (`shouldUseArgvSpawn`), never an actual win32 spawn — so the synchronous EINVAL regression is invisible to CI.
+
+This is the same regression class N1 rejected, only partially fixed, and the code comment states a claim that is factually wrong on Node/win32. Not a security escalation (argv mode is fail-closed; the error is caught upstream at server.ts:2242), but it is a functional regression on the primary platform with an incorrect "safe" claim — failing the "reject if incomplete claims" bar.
+
+### Nits
+- `downloads-find.ts:198–201`: `count` reports trimmed length while the conflict hint scans up to 20 matches — hint may reference rows absent from the returned array (N1 N2, still open).
+- `skill-install.test.ts`: the "content writes under skills root" test asserts `r.ok || r.error` (always true) and the stub engine's `skillsDir` ≠ real `getUserSkillsRoot()`, so `dest_path` containment vs. the real engine is not actually asserted.
+- `skill_install` case in server.ts:3243 writes/overwrites user skills with no audit line and no size cap on the `path` (folder) branch; acceptable for now (pre-existing engine behavior, engine dest only) but worth an audit line.
