+I've completed a full review of all four tracks. Here's my assessment:
+
+## Verification performed
+
+**Track 1 — FocusBand ST-4 + DL-4 + skill_install hints**
+- `resolveFocusBandSlot` order matches DoD exactly: Confirm → L2 → Fleet → `thread_tools` → L1 → empty (focus-band-priority.ts:60-112). Height budget respected: primary ≤56px + secondary ≤24px = ≤80px; `secondaryTools` is mutually exclusive with `secondaryAbort`/`secondaryContext`. ✓
+- Shared `collectRunningTools` used by both ChatView and FocusBand; dedupes by name, newest-first, 40-msg scan window. ✓
+- DL-4 conflict hints (`conflict_hint_zh`) implemented in downloads-find.ts with tests; note + tool description reference `skill_install` (track-3 hint). ✓
+
+**Track 2 — skill_install**
+- Server handler wired (server.ts:3242), tool injected into catalog via `ensureBrowserDownloadTool`. Destination is always `~/.cmspark-agent/skills` (config.ts:17 + skill-engine.ts:68). Engine's `importSkillFolder`/`importSkillFiles` have path-traversal protections (verified + existing tests at skills.test.ts:1066). Zip ≤25MB, `~` expansion, realpath (no symlink write escape). **No new Side Panel/manifest/UI entry** — only LLM tool + hint strings. ✓
+
+**Track 3 — shell P1b**
+- `tryParseSimpleArgv` returns null for metachars (incl. `$`), globs, `${`, `$var`, unclosed quotes. win32 argv mode restricted to `.exe`/`.com` (`.bat`/`.cmd`/bare names stay shell:true — tested). `spawn_mode` reported in result. Argv mode never reinterprets args (no shell), so this strictly *reduces* injection surface. ✓
+
+**Track 4 — Outbound MCP Phase 0**
+- Spike plan doc present with P0c status. Profile allowlist (8 curated `cmspark__` tools) is fail-closed: shell_exec/cookies/host/evaluate/skill_install → `PROFILE_FORBIDDEN`. Exfil class (`get_page_text`, `screenshot`) requires disclosure. Audit line on every call. No bridge — consistent with scoped "no full WS bridge". ✓
+
+**Tests:** 408 chrome-extension tests + 28 relevant companion tests pass (skill-install, outbound-mcp-facade, shell-progress-windowsHide, capability-shell-netsec). TS compiles clean.
+
+**Security:** No regression found. All four DoD gates hold.
+
+## Nits
+
+1. **companion/src/capability/shell.ts:168,174** — On non-win32, *any* parseable command goes argv mode, including POSIX builtins (`cd /tmp`, `export FOO=bar`, `source x`) and non-executable `./script.sh` (no +x), which now fail with ENOENT/EACCES where `sh -c` previously succeeded. The comment overclaims ("any successful parse… work with shell:false"). Mitigated by `spawn_mode` in results, but the shell_exec LLM tool description (unchanged) doesn't mention argv mode — agents may be surprised.
+2. **companion/src/skills/skill-install.ts:20,73** — `url` param is declared in `SkillInstallParams` but never handled (dead field); content-branch `dest_path` falls back to `root` when the file doesn't exist, which is misleading — return the actual written path.
+3. **chrome-extension/src/background/downloads-find.ts:185** — `Math.max(limit, 20)` is constant 20 (limit clamped ≤20 above); conflict scan covers only the first 20 filtered matches while the API query fetches 50 — harmless but misleading.
+4. **companion/tests/skill-install.test.ts** — the "content writes under skills root" test asserts `r.ok || r.error` (always true); tautology that passes even if content import silently broke. Assert the file actually landed in the engine's skillsDir.
+
+VERDICT: APPROVE_WITH_NITS
